# Brief first, then SM one ticket at a time

This repo has `require_brief: true`. Product, UX, and behavior changes go through dm-software-machine. Conversation is not a spec. Small UX nits are not exempt.

One-off questions (what does X do, why did Y fail) may stay in chat. Software implementations need a ticket.

## Stop

When the user asks to implement or change app behavior and there is no complete spec for that change:

1. `just sm-ticket "<one sentence>"` from the repo root (`markable/`). Pass their words as `--problem`. Fallback: `uv run dm-software-machine/scripts/dmsm.py task-ticket --new --title "…" --problem "…"`.
2. Their description is the brief. Translate it into Problem, In scope, Out of scope, UX / behavior, and Tests. The general idea is enough. Ask a question only when that description cannot be carried out.
3. Do not hand them a fill template. Do not add behavior they did not describe.
4. `just sm-ready <id>` once the translation is in the file. Do not `sm-claim` until the spec is ready. Do not edit `src/`, `src-tauri/`, `index.html`, `flavors/`, or other writes before claim.

## After the translation is in the file

`just sm-ready <id>`. They move the card. `sm-claim` stays a backup. Implement that ticket only. `sm-finish` then `sm-accept`. Auto-advance may claim the next **queued complete** ticket. Briefing tickets stay parked.

## Carve-outs

- Already-claimed SM task in a gate repair loop
- One-off questions or analysis with no code

The tracker is the built-in project store (`just sm-prime`, `just sm-board`).
